  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the most vulnerable individuals affected by the earthquake through the rehabilitation the vital markets</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim is to address the urgent needs of vulnerable groups affected by the earthquake in Aleppo governorates through a five-month initiative. This project seeks to provide essential assistance to internally displaced persons (IDPs) and households within host communities in Aleppo governorates. It specifically targets 19,400 households, comprising approximately 19,400 HHs - 97,000 individuals (65,000 HC and 32,000 IDPs), (men 21,340 women 23,280, boys 25,220, girls 27,160). with a focus on delivering life-saving aid with the following&#x2019;s activities:  Rehabilitation of Atareb vital markets in Atareb community: The vital markets are located in center of the community affected by the earthquake, the major reason for selecting Atareb markets because its key role in stimulating commercial activity, providing job opportunities, and serving the residents of the region with basic needs, The vital markets contain of 210 shops and very important in the region because it is visited by neighboring communities.</narrative>
  </description>
